{"term":"community","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:371922564ce79ccb49","definition":"A group sharing common characteristics, such as the same language, law, religion, or tradition.","example":"[W]e are not borne to our ſelues alone, but the prince, the countrie, the parents, freends, wiues, children and familie, euerie of them doo claime an intereſt in vs, and to euerie of them we muſt be beneficiall: otherwiſe we doo degenerate from that communitie and ſocietie, which by ſuch offices by vs is to be conſtrued, & doo become moſt vnprofitable: […]","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["anticommunity","noncommunity"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable","wordFamily":["aim community","anticommunity","autonomous community","bedroom community","biocommunity","care in the community","climax community","communitarian","communitarianism","communitization","communitize","community card","community cat","community centre","community chest","community college","community council","community development","community garden","community group","community immunity","community interest company","community language","community manager","community note","community nurse","community of practice","community organizer","community owned","community ownership"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/community#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a0d844e167df4cf389","definition":"A residential or religious collective; a commune.","example":"The Beguines, an uncloistered religiously inspired woman's movement began about the year 1210 in Liége, Belgium. Generally the Beguines lived in community or in small cottages behind a wall. At times threatened as heretics, they were finally disbanded by the Reformation.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["anticommunity","noncommunity"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable","wordFamily":["aim community","anticommunity","autonomous community","bedroom community","biocommunity","care in the community","climax community","communitarian","communitarianism","communitization","communitize","community card","community cat","community centre","community chest","community college","community council","community development","community garden","community group","community immunity","community interest company","community language","community manager","community note","community nurse","community of practice","community organizer","community owned","community ownership"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/community#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b2617a33b52ca936de","definition":"A group of interdependent organisms inhabiting the same region and interacting with each other.","example":"Synecology has for the objects of its study, not individual organisms but biological communities, which are groups of organisms living in a given space, the properties of which space select a certain assemblage of organisms of definite autecological characteristics. Such communities are moreover not merely collections of organisms of restricted autecology, but tend to become organized by the biotic relationships that exist beteen the various individuals comprising the community.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["anticommunity","noncommunity"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable","wordFamily":["aim community","anticommunity","autonomous community","bedroom community","biocommunity","care in the community","climax community","communitarian","communitarianism","communitization","communitize","community card","community cat","community centre","community chest","community college","community council","community development","community garden","community group","community immunity","community interest company","community language","community manager","community note","community nurse","community of practice","community organizer","community owned","community ownership"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/community#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:86acace6f1b704c011","definition":"A group of people interacting by electronic means for educational, professional, social, or other purposes; a virtual community.","example":"Spam texts are encoded but no decryption is possible. There is no plaintext message. I find them wonderful, and read them as poetics, as odd fragments generative of narrtives and scenography. I find the process of their production wonderful as well. The texts are written to elude community standards and means of censorship, and at the same time to enter and impose themselves into the standards and means for the community to read itself.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["anticommunity","noncommunity"],"collocations":[],"usage":"Internet","register":"Internet, countable","wordFamily":["aim community","anticommunity","autonomous community","bedroom community","biocommunity","care in the community","climax community","communitarian","communitarianism","communitization","communitize","community card","community cat","community centre","community chest","community college","community council","community development","community garden","community group","community immunity","community interest company","community language","community manager","community note","community nurse","community of practice","community organizer","community owned","community ownership"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/community#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5b0a8178652a2259ab","definition":"The condition of having certain attitudes and interests in common.","example":"We hope to demonstrate that Paul understood the local community to be the sphere in which and the means through which the five components of the maturation process were facilitated, thus concluding that Paul expected believers to be confirmed to Christ in community.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["anticommunity","noncommunity"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"uncountable","wordFamily":["aim community","anticommunity","autonomous community","bedroom community","biocommunity","care in the community","climax community","communitarian","communitarianism","communitization","communitize","community card","community cat","community centre","community chest","community college","community council","community development","community garden","community group","community immunity","community interest company","community language","community manager","community note","community nurse","community of practice","community organizer","community owned","community ownership"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/community#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:24aa646e836d0972d6","definition":"A feeling of togetherness or connectedness, common identity or of possessing a similar outlook, perspective and purpose with some group of people.","example":"Volunteering gave me a sense of community.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["anticommunity","noncommunity"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"uncountable","wordFamily":["aim community","anticommunity","autonomous community","bedroom community","biocommunity","care in the community","climax community","communitarian","communitarianism","communitization","communitize","community card","community cat","community centre","community chest","community college","community council","community development","community garden","community group","community immunity","community interest company","community language","community manager","community note",